"Calculated values (TEF, net Kcal, F/F ratio) are already included; in "
"updated rows the cells that change are highlighted."

#, python-format
msgid ""
"I valori che il CREA non pubblica vengono, in quest'ordine: dalla tabella"
" britannica <a href=\"%(url)s\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener "
"noreferrer\">CoFID 2021</a> (McCance and Widdowson, Public Health "
"England, <a href=\"%(licenza)s\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener "
"noreferrer\">Open Government Licence v3.0</a>) per il profilo degli "
"zuccheri di prodotti europei (e per gli zuccheri totali, se mancano anche"
" in USDA) e per i grassi saturi, come percentuale degli acidi grassi o "
"come quota sui grassi; poi dall'alimento corrispondente di USDA FoodData "
"Central (dominio pubblico) per gli altri campi. Gli abbinamenti sono "
"scelti alimento per alimento e la scheda indica quali valori vengono da "
"dove."
msgstr ""
"Values that CREA doesn't publish come, in this order: from the UK <a "
"href=\"%(url)s\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">CoFID "
"2021</a> table (McCance and Widdowson, Public Health England, <a "
"href=\"%(licenza)s\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Open "
"Government Licence v3.0</a>) for the sugar profile of European products "
"(and for total sugars, if USDA lacks them too) and for saturated fat, as "
"a percentage of fatty acids or as a share of the fat; then from the "
"matching USDA FoodData Central food (public domain) for the other fields."
" Matches are chosen food by food, and the food page shows which values "
"come from where."

